Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/cofflink.c
Line: 3026
Function: coff_relocate_section
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: sec = sections[symndx] indexes the sections array with symndx from the input relocation/symbol without any bounds check. A crafted object with an out-of-range symbol index can cause an out-of-bounds read when accessing sections[symndx], potentially leading to a crash later when sec is used.

Source context:
